// Sharpened altitude/speed reward scales for ultra-tight steady-state
// tracking (goal: mean_tail_abs_altitude_m <= 0.05 m, mean_tail_abs_speed_mps
// <= 0.05 m/s, i.e. error over the settled final 20% of each episode — see
// evaluate_policy's --task level_hold output).
//
// Produced by target/skill-runs/level_hold-goal-20260804-tight005 (a 2-batch,
// 8-parallel train_ppo search starting from the
// skill_level_hold_tight_tracking incumbent, see
// level_hold_tight_tracking.reward.ron). Winning checkpoint:
// models/level_hold/skill_level_hold_tight005b2_from40s3_samereward_lowlr_2M.mpk
// — reached mean_tail_abs_altitude_m=0.033 m, mean_tail_abs_speed_mps=0.014 m/s,
// success_rate=1.0 over 1000 eval episodes.
//
// Key finding: this reward config alone did not do it — a first-stage
// continuation under these scales (alt=40, speed=3, default lr=3e-4) only
// reached tail_alt=0.099/tail_speed=0.075. A *second* continuation from that
// checkpoint, same reward config, but with a 3x lower learning rate
// (see level_hold_ultra_tight_tracking.ppo.ron, lr=1e-4 vs default 3e-4) for
// another 2M steps is what closed the gap to <=0.05/<=0.05 — a low-LR
// fine-tune pass at a reward config the policy has already partially
// converged under, rather than a further-tightened reward. Tightening the
// reward scale further (down to alt=30/speed=1.5) at the default LR was
// consistently *worse* (regressed to tail_alt 0.1-0.8 range) — this reward
// landscape is noisy near convergence and aggressive scale changes can
// destabilize a nearly-converged policy. Not the default level_hold reward
// config; pass explicitly via
// --reward-config assets/training/level_hold_ultra_tight_tracking.reward.ron
// --ppo-config assets/training/level_hold_ultra_tight_tracking.ppo.ron.
//
// NOTE: the checkpoint and eval numbers above were all measured at a single fixed
// 1000 m / 100 m/s target, before target altitude/airspeed were randomized per-episode
// (LevelHoldEnv::with_target_ranges, default 500-5000 m / 90-140 m/s). A randomized-target
// run is a harder task and is not expected to reach the same tail-error numbers without
// its own retune.
(
    alt_error_scale:    40.0,
    alt_error_weight:   1.0,
    speed_error_scale:  3.0,
    speed_error_weight: 0.5,
    roll_scale:         0.5,
    roll_weight:        0.3,
    beta_scale:         0.5,
    beta_weight:        0.1,
    alive_bonus:        0.01,
    min_altitude:       10.0,
    max_altitude_error: 500.0,
    max_episode_steps:  3000,
)
